$ x^2 equiv 1 mod p &<=> x^2 - 1 equiv 0 mod p \
                    &<=> (x - 1)(x + 1) equiv 0 mod p \
                    &<=> p divides (x - 1)(x + 1) \
                    &<=> p divides (x - 1) "or" p divides (x + 1) \
                    &<=> x equiv 1 mod p "or" x equiv -1 mod p, $
where the fourth step applies Euclid's lemma to the prime $p$, and conversely.
